<description>
<![CDATA[ <p><p>Flowserve is the recognized world leader in supplying pumps, valves, seals, automation, and services to the power, oil, gas, chemical, and other industries. With more than 16,000 employees in over 50 countries, we combine our global reach with a local presence. Join a company with the most comprehensive product lines and broadest applications experience in the world. You'll be part of a team known for its industry-leading talent, unparalleled portfolio, and unmatched commitment to customer success. Our culture promotes recognition and rewards creativity, hard work, and commitment. We invite you to put your talents and experience in motion with Flowserve. Flowserve is an Equal Opportunity Employer.</p><p><br /><br /></p><h3><b>Position Description</b></h3><p>Flowserve is seeking a skilled Customer Product Repair Mechanic to drive hands-on teardown, inspection, reconditioning, and assembly of critical industrial equipment in an active, precision-driven Quick Response Center (QRC) environment. In this role, you will handle rotating machinery, industrial pumps, high-energy electric actuators, small compressors, and decoking systems. Your craftsmanship directly impacts equipment uptime and reliability for premier energy, industrial, and infrastructure customers.</p><p><br /><br /></p><h3><b>Accountabilities</b></h3><ul><li style="color:#1f1f1f !important"><span style="color:#1f1f1f">Disassemble, inspect, recondition, and rebuild industrial rotating equipment, pumps, compressors, decoking hardware, and high-energy electric actuators according to engineering drawings and work routers.</span></li></ul><p> </p><ul><li style="color:#1f1f1f !important"><span style="color:#1f1f1f">Perform Disassembly, Cleaning, and Inspection (DCI) processes; document component wear and failure modes, photograph parts per checklist standards, and complete inspection reports prior to quotation.</span></li></ul><p> </p><ul><li style="color:#1f1f1f !important"><span style="color:#1f1f1f">Accurately set up and utilize precision measuring instruments—including micrometers, dial indicators, calipers, and bore gauges—to verify critical fits, tolerances, and run-outs.</span></li></ul><p> </p><ul><li style="color:#1f1f1f !important"><span style="color:#1f1f1f">Operate dynamic balancing equipment to precision-balance rotating assemblies and components.</span></li></ul><p> </p><ul><li style="color:#1f1f1f !important"><span style="color:#1f1f1f">Execute quality assurance testing, including low-pressure pneumatic leak tests and high-pressure hydrostatic pressure tests.</span></li></ul><p> </p><ul><li style="color:#1f1f1f !important"><span style="color:#1f1f1f">Safely apply thermal fits using controlled heat sources (torches/induction heaters) and liquid nitrogen for bearing and sleeve installations.</span></li></ul><p> </p><ul><li style="color:#1f1f1f !important"><span style="color:#1f1f1f">Operate overhead bridge cranes, hoists, rigging hardware, and forklifts to position heavy industrial assemblies safely.</span></li></ul><p> </p><ul><li style="color:#1f1f1f !important"><span style="color:#1f1f1f">Finish, paint, install industrial tagging, and prep completed machinery for outgoing customer shipment.</span></li></ul><p> </p><ul><li style="color:#1f1f1f !important"><span style="color:#1f1f1f">Collaborate cross-functionally with production planners, service coordinators, application engineers, and customers regarding equipment condition and repair milestones.</span></li></ul><p> </p><ul><li style="color:#1f1f1f !important"><span style="color:#1f1f1f">Champion shop floor safety, actively participate in 5S and continuous improvement initiatives, and exercise Stop Work Authority when safety risks arise.</span></li></ul><p> </p><h3><b>Position Requirements</b></h3><p> </p><ul><li style="color:#1f1f1f !important"><span style="color:#1f1f1f">High School Diploma or GED equivalent.</span></li></ul><p> </p><ul><li style="color:#1f1f1f !important"><span style="color:#1f1f1f">Minimum of 3–5 years of hands-on mechanical repair, teardown, and assembly experience with industrial rotating equipment, pumps, or mechanical machinery.</span></li></ul><p> </p><ul><li style="color:#1f1f1f !important"><span style="color:#1f1f1f">Proven ability to read and interpret mechanical blueprints, engineering cross-sections, shop routers, and technical checklists.</span></li></ul><p> </p><ul><li style="color:#1f1f1f !important"><span style="color:#1f1f1f">Demonstrated proficiency using precision measurement tools (micrometers, calipers, dial indicators) and documenting critical fits/clearances.</span></li></ul><p> </p><ul><li style="color:#1f1f1f !important"><span style="color:#1f1f1f">Working knowledge of electrical wiring or electromechanical assembly.</span></li></ul><p> </p><ul><li style="color:#1f1f1f !important"><span style="color:#1f1f1f">Ownership of a standard personal roll-around toolbox and basic hand/measurement tools.</span></li></ul><p> </p><ul><li style="color:#1f1f1f !important"><span style="color:#1f1f1f">Basic computer literacy, including navigation of work order systems and Microsoft Office.</span></li></ul><p> </p><ul><li style="color:#1f1f1f !important"><span style="color:#1f1f1f">Physical capability to stand for extended periods, maneuver tools, and lift up to 25 pounds, with schedule flexibility to work overtime and weekend shifts as customer repair demands require.</span></li></ul><p> </p><p><b>Preferred Qualifications:</b></p><p><br /><br /></p><ul><li style="color:#1f1f1f !important"><span style="color:#1f1f1f">Direct experience with valve automation, electric actuation, or hydraulic/pneumatic controls.</span></li></ul><p> </p><ul><li style="color:#1f1f1f !important"><span style="color:#1f1f1f">Background working in a fast-paced field service, aftermarket QRC, or dynamic pump/compressor overhaul facility.</span></li></ul><p> </p><ul><li style="color:#1f1f1f !important"><span style="color:#1f1f1f">Experience conducting hydrostatic pressure testing and operating dynamic balancing machinery.</span></li></ul><p> </p><h3><b>What We Can Offer You</b></h3><p>At Flowserve, you'll find a range of options to fit your, and your family's, needs. We want to provide our team with the right resources to invest in your physical, mental, and financial well-being no matter where you sit or what stage of life you're in.</p><p> </p><p>Our benefits include:</p><p><br /><br /></p><ul><li style="color:#1f1f1f !important"><span style="color:#1f1f1f">Competitive Hourly Pay with Overtime Opportunities</span></li></ul><p> </p><ul><li style="color:#1f1f1f !important"><span style="color:#1f1f1f">Tool and Safety Equipment Allowances</span></li></ul><p> </p><ul><li style="color:#1f1f1f !important"><span style="color:#1f1f1f">Medical, Dental & Vision Insurance</span></li></ul><p> </p><ul><li style="color:#1f1f1f !important"><span style="color:#1f1f1f">401(k) Retirement Savings Plan with Company Match</span></li></ul><p> </p><ul><li style="color:#1f1f1f !important"><span style="color:#1f1f1f">Flexible Spending Account (FSA) and Health Savings Account (HSA)</span></li></ul><p> </p><ul><li style="color:#1f1f1f !important"><span style="color:#1f1f1f">Short- and Long-Term Disability</span></li></ul><p> </p><ul><li style="color:#1f1f1f !important"><span style="color:#1f1f1f">Paid Time Off (PTO) and Company-Paid Holidays</span></li></ul><p> </p><ul><li style="color:#1f1f1f !important"><span style="color:#1f1f1f">Parental Leave</span></li></ul><p> </p><ul><li style="color:#1f1f1f !important"><span style="color:#1f1f1f">Life, Supplemental Life, Child, Spousal, and AD&D Insurance</span></li></ul></p> ]]>
</description>
